                <pb facs="0258" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.00/792: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-08-24T17:00:00-05:00">August 24, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 25—1:48 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. At personal request of Mrs. Ayora President and family are my guests in this
                    Legation. Granting of temporary sanctuary is in my opinion fully justified until
                    danger to personal safety of President has passed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
